WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.564
Gate 2's first step is to choose
one writer per attribute,

2
00:00:03.564 --> 00:00:06.925
and the guide offers two
patterns, as design guidance.

3
00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:10.425
In the first, Entra inbound
provisioning stays the door.

4
00:00:10.425 --> 00:00:15.233
SailPoint aggregates HR read-only,
and governs entitlements:

5
00:00:15.233 --> 00:00:19.475
groups, roles, access packages
and application access.

6
00:00:19.475 --> 00:00:23.307
In the second, SailPoint becomes
the provisioning service,

7
00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:25.887
and takes on Book 03's middleware duties.

8
00:00:25.887 --> 00:00:27.599
Pick one and write it down.

9
00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:28.575
Not both.

10
00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:32.825
Then record each attribute's writer
in the program's attribute map.

11
00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:38.542
One fact helps the choice: SailPoint's
Oracle HCM Cloud connector reads Core HCM

12
00:00:38.542 --> 00:00:41.660
directly, without an
on-premises appliance,

13
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.125
and writes back only the
user name and work email.

14
00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:50.470
For the first pattern's build, the guide
points to its Oracle HCM to Entra guide.
